---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About - Juan Contreras"
  description="Industrial engineer and game programmer in Detroit - B.S. Industrial & Systems Engineering (UM-Dearborn), B.S. Game Development (Full Sail valedictorian), and fabrication-floor, estimating, and software experience at a Michigan manufacturer."
  current="about"
>
  <section class="section about">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">// about</span>
      <h1 class="section-title">Hi, I'm Juan</h1>
      <div class="about-body">
        <p>
          I'm an industrial engineer and game programmer in Detroit with two bachelor's degrees and a habit of owning
          problems end to end. Industrial &amp; systems engineering came first - processes, measurement, continuous
          improvement - and it shapes how I work on everything: learn how the system really runs, measure it, and
          change only what the data supports.
        </p>
        <p>
          At UM-Dearborn I studied manufacturing processes, facilities design, simulation, Six Sigma, human factors,
          operations research, and engineering economy, and finished with a two-semester
          <a href="/engineering/pharmacy-redesign">senior design capstone</a> redesigning a working pharmacy, where I
          led the ergonomics and human factors work.
        </p>
        <p>
          Then I went back for a second degree. At Full Sail I graduated <strong>valedictorian</strong> in Game
          Development (computer science focus), finishing the final year while working 40 hours a week. The program
          ran like a studio - five-person Scrum teams, sprint deadlines, and code that had to survive QA - and I built
          C++ combat and AI systems on a custom Vulkan stack, gameplay systems in Unity, and save/UI systems in Unreal
          Engine 5.
        </p>
        <p>
          Since March 2025 I've worked at The Wooden Stone, a Michigan countertop manufacturer. I'm on the fabrication
          floor every week, I support estimating and bid preparation from product drawings, and I build the
          <a href="/engineering/wooden-stone">estimating and operations software</a> the shop runs on - the place where
          both degrees meet.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="about-heading">Education</h2>
      <div class="edu-grid">
        <div class="edu-card">
          <h3>B.S., Industrial &amp; Systems Engineering</h3>
          <p class="edu-school">University of Michigan-Dearborn - April 2023</p>
          <p class="edu-detail">Manufacturing processes, facilities design, simulation (Arena), Six Sigma &amp; SPC, human factors &amp; ergonomics, operations research, engineering economy; two-semester senior design capstone</p>
        </div>
        <div class="edu-card">
          <h3>B.S., Game Development <span class="edu-focus">(Computer Science)</span></h3>
          <p class="edu-school">Full Sail University - March 2026</p>
          <p class="edu-detail"><strong>Valedictorian</strong> · 3.76 GPA · coursework from data structures and OS to graphics, networks, databases, and AI</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="about-heading">Experience</h2>
      <div class="edu-card exp-card">
        <h3>Web Development &amp; IT Manager - The Wooden Stone, LLC</h3>
        <p class="edu-school">Clinton Township, MI (custom countertop manufacturer) · March 2025 - present</p>
        <ul class="exp-bullets">
          <li>On the fabrication floor every week; estimating and bid preparation from product drawings, templates, and material specifications</li>
          <li>Wrote the estimating engine - shop-capacity limits, CNC machine time, trip planning, landed material cost - in the operations platform built with the project manager; 1,400+ automated tests</li>
          <li>Technical point of contact: diagnosis, root-cause analysis, and fixes across shop equipment, websites, infrastructure, and internal tooling</li>
          <li>Two production customer-facing sites; automation cutting manual data entry ~30%; reliability infrastructure (NAS, RAID 1, UPS-triggered safe shutdown)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2 class="about-heading">How I work</h2>
      <ul class="work-list">
        <li>Measure before changing anything - and check the tools first: on the capstone, I verified Siemens Jack against a hand posture analysis before trusting it</li>
        <li>Documented Git branching strategies my teams actually followed - I wrote the workflow doc on Nutty Pursuit</li>
        <li>Jira epics with story points and acceptance criteria; Scrum through Alpha, Beta, and QA sprints</li>
        <li>Testing as a habit - 50+ case suites in school, 1,400+ tests on the estimating engine - plus code reviews and changelogs</li>
        <li>Root-cause fixes as a discipline - every case study on this site includes a real bug or decision story</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-body {
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .about-body p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .about-body strong,
  .edu-detail strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .about-heading {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    text-transform: lowercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    margin-top: 2.8rem;
  }

  .about-heading::before {
    content: '// ';
    color: var(--red-text);
  }

  .edu-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
  }

  .edu-card {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.4rem 1.5rem;
  }

  .edu-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .edu-focus {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .edu-school {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--red-text);
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
  }

  .edu-detail {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
  }

  .exp-card {
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
  }

  .exp-bullets {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: 0.9rem 0 0 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .work-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .work-list li {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    padding-left: 1.3rem;
    position: relative;
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
  }

  .work-list li::before {
    content: '▸';
    color: var(--red-text);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .edu-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
